- [All] Conform. Conform.
- Who is happy to care
for her children,

512
00:20:21,922 --> 00:20:23,390
and they are thankful

513
00:20:23,423 --> 00:20:25,658
for their happiness
and security.

514
00:20:25,692 --> 00:20:27,527
When I accepted
the woman in me--

515
00:20:27,560 --> 00:20:29,697
--want to meet
your mother, james.

516
00:20:29,730 --> 00:20:32,232
We want to know the woman
who has inspired

517
00:20:32,265 --> 00:20:33,500
this splendid essay.

518
00:20:33,533 --> 00:20:34,768
Joan crawford?

519
00:20:34,802 --> 00:20:36,770
The committee of mothers
is meeting here tomorrow

520
00:20:36,803 --> 00:20:38,005
at 11:00.

521
00:20:38,038 --> 00:20:39,673
- Oh, it's b.Y.O.M.
- To discuss plans

522
00:20:39,707 --> 00:20:41,975
for the graduation
exercises.

523
00:20:42,008 --> 00:20:43,343
And we'd love
to have your mother

524
00:20:43,377 --> 00:20:45,178
serve on the committee,
james.

525
00:20:45,212 --> 00:20:47,547
I don't have a mom,
my dog ate her.

526
00:20:47,580 --> 00:20:49,582
Very well, james.

527
00:20:49,615 --> 00:20:51,050
Oh boy, oh boy,
I won, I won!

528
00:20:51,083 --> 00:20:52,452
After 11 years
in high school,

529
00:20:52,485 --> 00:20:54,220
I finally won!...Something.

530
00:20:54,253 --> 00:20:56,288
- Hey, everybody
lives in that house.
- Yeah.

531
00:20:56,322 --> 00:20:58,125
Mom! Mom!

532
00:20:58,158 --> 00:20:59,392
Oh, mom--

533
00:20:59,425 --> 00:21:02,295
oh no, mom's
in the bottle again!

534
00:21:02,328 --> 00:21:05,498
Eh, looks like mom invited
joe e. Lewis over again.

535
00:21:07,667 --> 00:21:10,003
Well, she tidied up
the place.

536
00:21:14,908 --> 00:21:16,377
Hmm.
"Went to store,

537
00:21:16,410 --> 00:21:18,712
"scotch in fridge.
Love, mom."

538
00:21:20,847 --> 00:21:23,683
"Buy yourself
another mother."

539
00:21:23,717 --> 00:21:25,752
It says "p.S. Say yes

540
00:21:25,785 --> 00:21:28,522
to martini and rossi
on the rocks-- say yes."

541
00:21:30,123 --> 00:21:31,825
Didn't cross her t.

542
00:21:31,858 --> 00:21:33,660
Jeez, her handwriting
is terrible!

543
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:42,368
She drank all the gin.

544
00:21:44,637 --> 00:21:46,640
Huh, ironically,
the humorful part

545
00:21:46,673 --> 00:21:48,408
is he buys liquor
with the ten bucks.

546
00:21:48,442 --> 00:21:50,810
- D'oh!
- He does.

547
00:21:50,843 --> 00:21:53,180
Where do I start?
It all looks so good.

548
00:21:53,213 --> 00:21:56,550
The vodka clashes with
the coffee table.

549
00:21:56,583 --> 00:21:57,817
Mom is hot!

550
00:21:57,850 --> 00:21:59,418
- [Bots growl]
- Hello, jimmy.

551
00:21:59,452 --> 00:22:01,522
- Oh, hello, shirley.
- Is your mother home?

552
00:22:01,555 --> 00:22:03,022
- No, she isn't.
- Oh, never mind.

553
00:22:03,055 --> 00:22:04,858
I didn't want
to see her especially.

554
00:22:04,892 --> 00:22:06,258
Besides, I can
see her later.

555
00:22:06,292 --> 00:22:07,793
Okay, who are you?

556
00:22:07,827 --> 00:22:10,163
You can offer me a drink
if you wanna.

557
00:22:10,197 --> 00:22:11,432
And I think you wanna.

558
00:22:11,465 --> 00:22:12,598
Sure, help yourself.

559
00:22:12,632 --> 00:22:14,533
- Just pick a table.
- Thanks.

560
00:22:14,567 --> 00:22:17,203
It's a booze progressive
dinner, here.

561
00:22:17,237 --> 00:22:18,538
Well, how about you?

562
00:22:18,572 --> 00:22:19,940
Come on, join me.

563
00:22:19,973 --> 00:22:21,408
Can't do any more
than kill you.

564
00:22:21,442 --> 00:22:22,842
No thanks, not for me.

565
00:22:22,875 --> 00:22:24,677
I've been hitting it
too hard, lately.

566
00:22:24,710 --> 00:22:26,278
Yeah, I know,
it's kind of tough

567
00:22:26,312 --> 00:22:27,680
when it gets
the best of you.

568
00:22:27,713 --> 00:22:30,350
Well, here goes
for both of us.

569
00:22:30,383 --> 00:22:33,253
Hey, that's my booze.

570
00:22:33,287 --> 00:22:35,555
Looks like you're having
yourselves a time, you too.

571
00:22:35,588 --> 00:22:36,957
Suddenly,
the thin man enters.

572
00:22:36,990 --> 00:22:38,258
What goes on here?

573
00:22:38,292 --> 00:22:39,827
This is my first.

574
00:22:39,860 --> 00:22:41,828
- I wouldn't know about jim.
- Beam.

575
00:22:41,862 --> 00:22:43,997
- Mother home yet?
- No.

576
00:22:44,030 --> 00:22:45,765
Means another cold supper,
I suppose.

577
00:22:45,798 --> 00:22:47,567
Vodka sandwiches.

578
00:22:47,600 --> 00:22:49,635
What can you expect?
Nine times out of ten,

579
00:22:49,668 --> 00:22:51,838
if she did stay home
all day cooking,

580
00:22:51,872 --> 00:22:53,807
you'd phone the last minute
you had a business date

581
00:22:53,840 --> 00:22:55,508
- and couldn't make it.
- You the greek chorus?

582
00:22:55,542 --> 00:22:57,810
You women certainly
stick together, don't you?

583
00:22:57,843 --> 00:22:59,813
Not necessarily.

584
00:22:59,847 --> 00:23:01,948
I'd rather stick
to an attractive man.

585
00:23:01,982 --> 00:23:03,750
Dad, do you mind?

586
00:23:03,783 --> 00:23:06,653
Whoop, warden.

587
00:23:06,687 --> 00:23:08,388
Home so early, dan?

588
00:23:08,422 --> 00:23:10,090
I was a half hour late.

589
00:23:10,123 --> 00:23:12,292
But I was only detained
on business.

590
00:23:12,325 --> 00:23:14,693
You probably had
more important things to do.

591
00:23:14,727 --> 00:23:16,028
You needn't be
so cross about it.

592
00:23:16,062 --> 00:23:17,530
I'm sorry if I'm late.

593
00:23:17,563 --> 00:23:20,067
But the buses are so crowded,
and I couldn't get a taxi.

594
00:23:20,100 --> 00:23:22,035
I suppose you couldn't've
tried an hour earlier.

595
00:23:22,068 --> 00:23:23,403
No, I couldn't.

596
00:23:23,437 --> 00:23:25,505
Fix mother a drink, james.
I'm-- I'm exhausted.

597
00:23:25,538 --> 00:23:26,840
From drinking so much.

598
00:23:26,873 --> 00:23:28,542
Are we gonna have
any dinner tonight?

599
00:23:28,575 --> 00:23:30,477
In a minute,
it's all in the ice box.

600
00:23:30,510 --> 00:23:32,812
Hey, could somebody please
do an intervention?

601
00:23:32,845 --> 00:23:34,380
- --Shirley?
- Oh, no thanks.

602
00:23:34,413 --> 00:23:35,615
I have a date.

603
00:23:35,648 --> 00:23:37,983
- Another time, then.
- Thanks.

604
00:23:38,017 --> 00:23:39,552
- Ready for our date?
- Well,

605
00:23:39,585 --> 00:23:41,420
may the best man win.

606
00:23:41,453 --> 00:23:43,022
Who is that?

607
00:23:43,055 --> 00:23:44,623
I've had just about
enough of this.

608
00:23:44,657 --> 00:23:46,125
I won't put up
with it any longer.

609
00:23:46,158 --> 00:23:48,462
- What're you talking about?
- The whole setup!

610
00:23:48,495 --> 00:23:50,030
No decent meals on time.

611
00:23:50,063 --> 00:23:51,463
The house is always
in a mess.

612
00:23:51,497 --> 00:23:53,333
While you're gadding about,
making a fool of yourself.

613
00:23:53,367 --> 00:23:54,733
- I got an "a"--
- you do what you please.

614
00:23:54,767 --> 00:23:56,002
Why shouldn't I do
what I please?

615
00:23:56,035 --> 00:23:57,470
- That's okay with me.
- The teacher said--

616
00:23:57,503 --> 00:23:59,272
but you're not going
to do it while you're my wife.

617
00:23:59,305 --> 00:24:00,673
That suits me.

618
00:24:00,707 --> 00:24:02,475
You don't suppose I like
going on like this, do you?

619
00:24:02,508 --> 00:24:04,177
I'd've divorced you years ago
if it hadn't been for jimmy.

620
00:24:04,210 --> 00:24:05,512
Mother, dad, please.

621
00:24:05,545 --> 00:24:07,280
A flood of help
you've been to him.

622
00:24:07,313 --> 00:24:09,148
A fine home you've
made for him.

623
00:24:09,182 --> 00:24:10,483
- But I got a--
- well, how about
the example

624
00:24:10,517 --> 00:24:12,585
you've set him?
Out gambling every night.

625
00:24:12,618 --> 00:24:14,320
Sometimes not even
coming home at all.

626
00:24:14,353 --> 00:24:16,255
- Really good paper--
- a man has to do something
to pass the time.

627
00:24:16,288 --> 00:24:18,358
- Teacher said I was--

628
00:24:18,392 --> 00:24:20,360
- then why do you come home?
- Maybe I won't in the future.

629
00:24:20,393 --> 00:24:21,962
- But I can't--
- dad.

630
00:24:21,995 --> 00:24:23,330
- Freshen your drink?
- I've got something
to say to you.

631
00:24:23,363 --> 00:24:24,697
- Yeah son?
- It's something
about school.

632
00:24:24,730 --> 00:24:26,600
I won the essay contest,
and the principal said--

633
00:24:26,633 --> 00:24:28,768
well, say, that's fine.

634
00:24:28,802 --> 00:24:31,037
Here's $5.
Go out and celebrate.

635
00:24:31,070 --> 00:24:32,838
Spend it on
loose leaf paper.

636
00:24:32,872 --> 00:24:35,342
There goes a great man.

637
00:24:35,375 --> 00:24:37,710
What about my $5?

638
00:24:39,012 --> 00:24:40,147
Oh, jeez.

639
00:24:40,180 --> 00:24:41,715
This guy's made
more money today

640
00:24:41,748 --> 00:24:43,250
than I did all the way
through high school.

641
00:24:43,283 --> 00:24:45,052
- He'll be back.
- With another woman.

642
00:24:45,085 --> 00:24:47,320
I don't care
if he comes back or not.

643
00:24:47,353 --> 00:24:48,522
Won't be any different
if he does.

644
00:24:48,555 --> 00:24:49,788
Well, maybe it will.

645
00:24:49,822 --> 00:24:51,190
You see, I didn't tell dad
all that happened

646
00:24:51,223 --> 00:24:52,325
at school today.

647
00:24:52,358 --> 00:24:53,460
The principal
wants you to meet with

648
00:24:53,493 --> 00:24:55,695
the parents graduation committee
tomorrow at 11.

649
00:24:55,728 --> 00:24:57,997
Mrs. Carlyle and mrs. Whitney
are gonna be there.

650
00:24:58,030 --> 00:24:59,698
All the most important women
in the neighborhood.

651
00:24:59,732 --> 00:25:01,602
- Is there a bar?
- Oh, jimmy.

652
00:25:01,635 --> 00:25:03,237
--And they really
want me to be there?

653
00:25:03,270 --> 00:25:05,572
Oh, sure they do,
and I want you to go, mom.

654
00:25:05,605 --> 00:25:08,542
Yeah, they need
a laughingstock.

655
00:25:08,575 --> 00:25:10,877
I could wear my new
afternoon dress.

656
00:25:10,910 --> 00:25:12,745
And that hat I just bought.

657
00:25:12,778 --> 00:25:14,982
Oh, wait till he gets
the bill for that hat.

658
00:25:23,590 --> 00:25:25,592
Okay, so, is everybody done

659
00:25:25,625 --> 00:25:27,260
with their
art therapy project?

660
00:25:27,293 --> 00:25:28,528
Joel, what's the point

661
00:25:28,562 --> 00:25:30,230
of this art therapy stuff
anyway, huh?

662
00:25:30,263 --> 00:25:31,965
Well, by having you
draw pictures

663
00:25:31,998 --> 00:25:35,002
of your idealized family,
maybe you can escape

664
00:25:35,035 --> 00:25:37,170
some of the deep
psychological problems

665
00:25:37,203 --> 00:25:39,072
that jimmy,
the star of today's movie,

666
00:25:39,105 --> 00:25:40,440
suffer because
of his family.

667
00:25:40,473 --> 00:25:41,975
So let's see what
you've drawn, okay?

668
00:25:42,008 --> 00:25:43,277
This is crow's.

669
00:25:43,310 --> 00:25:45,312
That's my dad.
He's all-powerful.

670
00:25:45,345 --> 00:25:47,147
His hands are made
of stainless steel,

671
00:25:47,180 --> 00:25:48,348
and he has lasers that

672
00:25:48,382 --> 00:25:50,217
shoot out of his chest.
Pew-pew!

673
00:25:50,250 --> 00:25:51,818
I don't have to tell you
he's the coolest dad

674
00:25:51,852 --> 00:25:53,052
in the whole neighborhood.

675
00:25:53,085 --> 00:25:55,122
And we-- when we go
to father-son picnics,

676
00:25:55,155 --> 00:25:56,723
we win every event.

677
00:25:56,757 --> 00:25:58,425
And he dispenses
homespun wisdom,

678
00:25:58,458 --> 00:26:00,260
and teaches
solid midwestern values

679
00:26:00,293 --> 00:26:02,028
while crushing all
who block his path.

680
00:26:02,062 --> 00:26:05,065
Uh-huh, what about
the handlebar mustache?

681
00:26:05,098 --> 00:26:06,198
I don't know.

682
00:26:06,232 --> 00:26:07,767
O-kay.

683
00:26:07,800 --> 00:26:09,068
Let's see here.

684
00:26:09,102 --> 00:26:12,738
Uh, oral obsession
with mustache

685
00:26:12,772 --> 00:26:15,942
indicates
nasal-labial shame.

686
00:26:15,975 --> 00:26:17,477
- Sounds serious.
- Okay.

687
00:26:17,510 --> 00:26:19,712
Now let's see yours here.
Tom, what's this?

688
00:26:19,745 --> 00:26:22,315
Okey-doke, uh,
that's my mom, my dad,

689
00:26:22,348 --> 00:26:24,650
and my mom.
My mom is hayley mills,

690
00:26:24,683 --> 00:26:27,653
my dad is gigantor,
and my mom is peggy cass.

691
00:26:27,687 --> 00:26:31,423
Uh-huh, and why are your moms
holding hands, tom?

692
00:26:31,457 --> 00:26:32,525
I don't know.

693
00:26:32,558 --> 00:26:33,960
O-kay.

694
00:26:33,993 --> 00:26:37,530
Let's see, latent
parent-trap syndrome.

695
00:26:37,563 --> 00:26:39,465
Man should be
in a straitjacket.

696
00:26:39,498 --> 00:26:41,633
Okay, gypsy, well,
this one's really nice.

697
00:26:41,667 --> 00:26:42,902
What's this one?

698
00:26:42,935 --> 00:26:45,772
Joel, my ideal family
is right here.

699
00:26:45,805 --> 00:26:48,508
And I know richard basehart
watches over us all.

700
00:26:48,542 --> 00:26:49,742
- Huh.
- Oh...

701
00:26:49,775 --> 00:26:51,778
That's really sweet, gypsy,
but tell me--

702
00:26:51,812 --> 00:26:54,113
why does richard basehart
get to play god?

703
00:26:54,147 --> 00:26:55,382
I don't know.

704
00:26:55,415 --> 00:26:56,817
Joel, why are you
spending your time

705
00:26:56,850 --> 00:26:58,150
psychoanalyzing robots?

706
00:26:58,183 --> 00:27:00,487
Um... I don't know.

707
00:27:00,520 --> 00:27:02,388
I'm kidding, of course.
We'll be right back.

708
00:27:02,422 --> 00:27:04,190
I do know.
I really do know.

709
00:27:11,297 --> 00:27:13,265
[Dan laughs]

710
00:27:13,298 --> 00:27:14,533
What? What's so funny?

711
00:27:14,567 --> 00:27:15,835
That joe bolster.

712
00:27:15,868 --> 00:27:17,103
He just cracks me up.

713
00:27:17,137 --> 00:27:18,972
The mirror
ought to tell you.

714
00:27:19,005 --> 00:27:20,940
I'm getting ready
to go to jim's school.

715
00:27:20,973 --> 00:27:23,377
Well, you certainly
look the part.

716
00:27:23,410 --> 00:27:25,812
Why don't you act your age?

717
00:27:25,845 --> 00:27:27,447
Stop criticizing me.

718
00:27:27,480 --> 00:27:29,615
You don't like my clothes.
You don't like my hat.

719
00:27:29,648 --> 00:27:30,850
You don't like it
if I sit around here.

720
00:27:30,883 --> 00:27:32,118
You don't like it
if I go out.

721
00:27:32,152 --> 00:27:34,020
Oh, let's stop
this ridiculous farce.

722
00:27:34,053 --> 00:27:35,188
Why don't we quit?

723
00:27:35,222 --> 00:27:37,157
- I-- I like your hat.
- Great idea.

724
00:27:37,190 --> 00:27:38,792
Thanks for the suggestion.

725
00:27:38,825 --> 00:27:41,762
So they're divorced now?
That was easy.

726
00:27:41,795 --> 00:27:43,362
Hmm, he's a good husband.

727
00:27:43,395 --> 00:27:45,998
He just has a hard time
expressing his feelings.

728
00:27:47,867 --> 00:27:51,838
She's got a sea anemone
on her head.

729
00:27:51,872 --> 00:27:54,573
♪ Mirror mirror
on the wall ♪

730
00:27:54,607 --> 00:27:56,542
Can I make it to last call?

731
00:27:58,812 --> 00:28:00,380
I'm gonna work on
the decorating committee.

732
00:28:00,413 --> 00:28:01,647
Oh, isn't that swell?

733
00:28:01,680 --> 00:28:03,483
Some of us girls thought
we could bring some flowers.

734
00:28:03,517 --> 00:28:05,285
I'm gonna build a blimp
and fight the nazis.

735
00:28:05,318 --> 00:28:06,652
--To win the contest.

736
00:28:06,685 --> 00:28:09,188
I think he should read it at
the graduation exercises.

737
00:28:09,222 --> 00:28:10,623
Why, yes, what
an excellent idea.

738
00:28:10,657 --> 00:28:12,058
Wow, the whole school
seems to be

739
00:28:12,092 --> 00:28:13,527
buzzing about that essay.

740
00:28:13,560 --> 00:28:14,727
--My home, that's all.

741
00:28:14,760 --> 00:28:16,395
It's the way
any other fella's is.

742
00:28:16,428 --> 00:28:17,663
The way a home ought to be.

743
00:28:17,697 --> 00:28:19,265
A very happy home,
obviously.

744
00:28:19,298 --> 00:28:21,067
I'm most anxious
to meet your mother.

745
00:28:21,100 --> 00:28:22,235
Oh, mom's swell.

746
00:28:22,268 --> 00:28:25,070
[All]
♪ liar! Liar! Liar! ♪

747
00:28:25,103 --> 00:28:26,940
--I had a lot
of brothers and sisters.

748
00:28:26,973 --> 00:28:28,942
She must take
a great interest in her home.

749
00:28:28,975 --> 00:28:30,377
She does. That's all
she thinks about.

750
00:28:30,410 --> 00:28:31,912
Oh, that and twist-off caps.

751
00:28:31,945 --> 00:28:34,080
What's more important when
you come right down to it?

752
00:28:34,113 --> 00:28:36,315
A woman's job is her home
and family, isn't it?

753
00:28:36,348 --> 00:28:38,050
At least, that's the way
my mom figures.

754
00:28:38,083 --> 00:28:40,320
Mrs.- hello everybody.
- Oh, and did I tell you
she drinks?

755
00:28:40,353 --> 00:28:41,922
Sorry if I'm late.

756
00:28:41,955 --> 00:28:44,423
Miss reardon drinks a lot.

757
00:28:44,457 --> 00:28:46,458
I'm jimmy wilson's mother.

758
00:28:46,492 --> 00:28:48,928
- [Giggles] She's drunk.
- It's funny!

759
00:28:48,962 --> 00:28:50,363
How shocking.

760
00:28:50,397 --> 00:28:52,165
Eleanor roosevelt's pissed.

761
