00:56:09,733 --> 00:56:11,402
Hey, you two
staying home tonight?

1501
00:56:11,435 --> 00:56:13,237
Hah, well, your father's
going to the club

1502
00:56:13,270 --> 00:56:14,505
to play cards later.

1503
00:56:14,538 --> 00:56:15,940
I thought you and I
might do something,

1504
00:56:15,973 --> 00:56:17,875
but I see you
have other plans.

1505
00:56:17,908 --> 00:56:20,112
- Oh, I'm sorry--
- he's dead!

1506
00:56:20,145 --> 00:56:21,645
Why don't you call up
one of your gang?

1507
00:56:21,678 --> 00:56:23,013
Maybe I will.

1508
00:56:23,047 --> 00:56:24,315
Well, goodbye now.

1509
00:56:24,348 --> 00:56:25,550
- Bye.
- [Dad groans]

1510
00:56:25,583 --> 00:56:27,318
[Crow mimics groan]

1511
00:56:27,352 --> 00:56:28,720
You think
he'd ever accuse us?

1512
00:56:28,753 --> 00:56:31,322
--Changed these last few weeks.
Have you noticed it, dan?

1513
00:56:31,355 --> 00:56:34,258
- Jimmy who?
- Yeah, he seems to have
grown up overnight.

1514
00:56:34,292 --> 00:56:35,960
Well, I don't like it.

1515
00:56:35,993 --> 00:56:38,428
What do you suppose he's doing
out every night in the week?

1516
00:56:38,462 --> 00:56:40,365
For several nights,
he didn't come home at all.

1517
00:56:40,398 --> 00:56:43,535
Maybe he stayed
with a friend.

1518
00:56:43,568 --> 00:56:46,170
It's a little late to start
asking questions now.

1519
00:56:46,203 --> 00:56:47,805
Well, after all,
your his father.

1520
00:56:47,838 --> 00:56:48,907
You ought to
keep an eye on him.

1521
00:56:48,940 --> 00:56:50,442
Well, you're his mother.

1522
00:56:50,475 --> 00:56:52,777
You stay home once in a while,
you might know what he's up to.

1523
00:56:52,810 --> 00:56:54,578
The talking corpse,
ladies and gentlemen.

1524
00:56:54,612 --> 00:56:56,580
--A girlfriend, that's all.

1525
00:56:56,613 --> 00:56:57,882
I had when I was his age.

1526
00:56:57,915 --> 00:56:59,417
And then I died inside.

1527
00:56:59,450 --> 00:57:01,185
--Taking after you.

1528
00:57:01,218 --> 00:57:03,120
That's it,
there's a six-pack

1529
00:57:03,153 --> 00:57:04,922
calling my name.

1530
00:57:10,662 --> 00:57:11,997
- Hello, kitty.
- Quack, quack, quack.

1531
00:57:12,030 --> 00:57:13,798
I brought you
a little something.

1532
00:57:13,832 --> 00:57:15,367
- Quack quack quack.
- Oh, jimmy.

1533
00:57:15,400 --> 00:57:16,935
- Leftover chinese!
- Not another present!

1534
00:57:16,968 --> 00:57:18,637
Why, sure. I like buying
presents for you.

1535
00:57:18,670 --> 00:57:20,672
- It's fun.
- But I always have
to pay for them.

1536
00:57:20,705 --> 00:57:22,840
Jimmy, I don't want you
to be offended,

1537
00:57:22,873 --> 00:57:24,108
but I've got
to ask you something.

1538
00:57:24,142 --> 00:57:25,743
Do I have a weird profile?

1539
00:57:25,777 --> 00:57:27,878
--Mixed up in anything that
isn't quite on the level,
are you?

1540
00:57:27,912 --> 00:57:29,113
Whatever gave you that idea?

1541
00:57:29,147 --> 00:57:30,815
I'm just selling drugs
to school kids.

1542
00:57:30,848 --> 00:57:33,150
--Except that you have so much
more money to spend lately.

1543
00:57:33,183 --> 00:57:34,585
- Oh, the mob ties.
- Look,

1544
00:57:34,618 --> 00:57:35,820
don't you worry about me.

1545
00:57:35,853 --> 00:57:37,188
I wouldn't do
anything that wasn't

1546
00:57:37,222 --> 00:57:38,723
on the right side
of the law.

1547
00:57:38,757 --> 00:57:40,258
I hope not, jimmy.

1548
00:57:40,292 --> 00:57:42,327
You're so sweet, I wouldn't
want you to change.

1549
00:57:42,360 --> 00:57:44,462
- Why should I change?
- I'll always wear
jed clampett's hat.

1550
00:57:44,495 --> 00:57:45,897
People do in this town.

1551
00:57:45,930 --> 00:57:48,700
- Circle pines'll do that.
- --You don't, kitty.

1552
00:57:48,733 --> 00:57:52,403
Now let me have
that tongue of yours.

1553
00:57:52,437 --> 00:57:53,672
Say, eddie mendez gave me

1554
00:57:53,705 --> 00:57:54,905
two tickets for
the follies sunday.

1555
00:57:54,938 --> 00:57:57,342
Hey, what do I bid for two
tickets to follies? Hey!

1556
00:57:57,375 --> 00:57:58,710
--Cancel that like you did
our luncheon date today?

1557
00:57:58,743 --> 00:58:01,045
Oh, now, look, kitten.
Can I help it if I'm busy?

1558
00:58:01,078 --> 00:58:02,413
I'm hanged
if I can find time

1559
00:58:02,447 --> 00:58:03,915
to do the things
we've planned.

1560
00:58:03,948 --> 00:58:05,417
But business
is sure picking up.

1561
00:58:05,450 --> 00:58:07,785
- Well, that's good.
- You bet, for both of us.

1562
00:58:07,818 --> 00:58:08,987
The higher
charlie blake goes...

1563
00:58:09,020 --> 00:58:10,755
- The higher kitty reed.
- You said it.

1564
00:58:10,788 --> 00:58:12,723
Well, bye, darling.

1565
00:58:12,757 --> 00:58:14,825
Oh, uh, I meant
to ask you before.

1566
00:58:14,858 --> 00:58:16,527
Have you put
jimmy wilson to work?

1567
00:58:16,560 --> 00:58:19,063
Why, uh, I haven't laid eyes
on him-- have you seen him?

1568
00:58:19,097 --> 00:58:21,365
[All] ♪ liar! Liar! ♪

1569
00:58:21,398 --> 00:58:22,900
--You asked me to give you
a buildup, remember?

1570
00:58:22,933 --> 00:58:24,102
Must've been a swell buildup

1571
00:58:24,135 --> 00:58:25,437
you gave him to
keep him away like this.

1572
00:58:25,470 --> 00:58:27,738
Man, everybody lies
in this movie.

1573
00:58:27,772 --> 00:58:29,540
--By now, he'd be pounding
on your door for a job.

1574
00:58:29,573 --> 00:58:30,775
Well, I haven't seen him.

1575
00:58:30,808 --> 00:58:32,143
I guess he's pounding
on the wrong door.

1576
00:58:32,177 --> 00:58:33,612
- You said it.
- Hey, you talk about

1577
00:58:33,645 --> 00:58:35,513
me giving you a stand-up--

1578
00:58:35,547 --> 00:58:37,782
where have you been disappearing
to after the show every night?

1579
00:58:37,815 --> 00:58:40,217
You sure get out of that
dressing room in a hurry.

1580
00:58:40,250 --> 00:58:41,485
And I've been missing you.

1581
00:58:41,518 --> 00:58:43,253
Well, charlie,
you know the old saying.

1582
00:58:43,287 --> 00:58:45,657
Early to bed
and early to rise.

1583
00:58:45,690 --> 00:58:47,958
- Huh?
- That's me. Bye, now.
- Goodbye.

1584
00:58:47,992 --> 00:58:49,627
I also know about
a bird in the hand.

1585
00:58:49,660 --> 00:58:52,297
Now, get out of here.
"Early to bed and early..."

1586
00:58:52,330 --> 00:58:53,932
You're new with mr. Blake.

1587
00:58:53,965 --> 00:58:55,467
How long have you
been with him?

1588
00:58:55,500 --> 00:58:57,435
A few weeks-- I'm not working
full-time for him yet.

1589
00:58:57,468 --> 00:58:59,003
Mmm, I see.

1590
00:58:59,037 --> 00:59:00,605
I'll be with you
in a minute.

1591
00:59:00,638 --> 00:59:03,107
Uh, note to self.
Find out correct time.

1592
00:59:05,643 --> 00:59:07,645
Uh, it's my birthday
tomorrow, mister.

1593
00:59:10,280 --> 00:59:12,417
What is this guy,
butcher to the mob?

1594
00:59:14,218 --> 00:59:15,853
Here you go.
Happy birthday, jimmy.

1595
00:59:15,887 --> 00:59:17,455
This is very important.

1596
00:59:17,488 --> 00:59:20,358
You see that mr. Blake
gets this note tonight.

1597
00:59:20,392 --> 00:59:22,760
And be sure that you
give it to no one but him.

1598
00:59:22,793 --> 00:59:23,995
All right, I'll do that.

1599
00:59:24,028 --> 00:59:27,498
And this is skag.
Be careful with it.

1600
00:59:27,532 --> 00:59:29,300
I'll let you out
the back door.

1601
00:59:29,333 --> 00:59:32,170
Don't tell the nazis
where I am.

1602
00:59:38,843 --> 00:59:40,010
Hi, I have
an important thing

1603
00:59:40,043 --> 00:59:42,647
and some stuff called skag?

1604
00:59:42,680 --> 00:59:43,915
What's the idea
coming back here?

1605
00:59:43,948 --> 00:59:45,248
I told you what to do
with that package.

1606
00:59:45,282 --> 00:59:47,152
I know you did, mr. Blake,
but mr. Carlton said

1607
00:59:47,185 --> 00:59:48,618
to give you this note.
He said it was important.

1608
00:59:48,652 --> 00:59:51,088
Is this a caper?

1609
00:59:51,122 --> 00:59:54,825
Never should've gone
to old country buffet with him.

1610
00:59:54,858 --> 00:59:56,227
Let's see,
what does it say here?

1611
00:59:56,260 --> 00:59:59,197
"Isn't this guy carrying
the letter a dink?"

1612
01:00:00,865 --> 01:00:02,700
It's all right, jimmy,
you did the right thing.

1613
01:00:02,733 --> 01:00:03,868
Better wait out
in the other office.

1614
01:00:03,902 --> 01:00:05,268
I may have something else
for you to do.

1615
01:00:05,302 --> 01:00:06,537
Okay, mr. Blake.

1616
01:00:06,570 --> 01:00:08,640
And, uh, do some filing
while you're out there.

1617
01:00:11,975 --> 01:00:14,345
Huh, yeah,
I got a real knack

1618
01:00:14,378 --> 01:00:16,913
for shadowy errands.
That's me.

1619
01:00:20,017 --> 01:00:21,218
All right, boys, come on in.

1620
01:00:21,252 --> 01:00:22,753
We're gonna
pants the courier.

1621
01:00:22,787 --> 01:00:24,522
William frawley!
Montgomery clift!

1622
01:00:24,555 --> 01:00:26,290
Get this. "Chuck,

1623
01:00:26,323 --> 01:00:27,558
"I tried to get the painting

1624
01:00:27,592 --> 01:00:29,193
"out of gordon's
dead storage.

1625
01:00:29,227 --> 01:00:31,362
"Couldn't make it as
the place is being watched.

1626
01:00:31,395 --> 01:00:33,197
"Don't send
any more packages.

1627
01:00:33,230 --> 01:00:35,600
"I'm leaving town.
Take my tip and do the same.

1628
01:00:35,633 --> 01:00:37,202
- Carl."
- well, how do you
like that?

1629
01:00:37,235 --> 01:00:39,270
- He called you chuck.
- I thought that stuff
was safe there.

1630
01:00:39,303 --> 01:00:41,038
$30,000 worth of diamonds.

1631
01:00:41,072 --> 01:00:42,307
What're you gonna
do now, charlie?

1632
01:00:42,340 --> 01:00:43,640
We're gonna talk
like dis, see?

1633
01:00:43,673 --> 01:00:44,875
-- To the warehouse
and get it out.

1634
01:00:44,908 --> 01:00:46,310
Tonight, and take
the kid with you.

1635
01:00:46,343 --> 01:00:47,812
Take the kid? What for?

1636
01:00:47,845 --> 01:00:49,280
May take two of you
to do the job.

1637
01:00:49,313 --> 01:00:50,882
I'll have him run a car,
and he can drive for you.

1638
01:00:50,915 --> 01:00:54,285
I'm due on
the superman set now.

1639
01:00:54,318 --> 01:00:55,653
- Oh, jimmy.
- Oh hi!

1640
01:00:55,687 --> 01:00:57,355
I want you to go down
to olson's before it closes

1641
01:00:57,388 --> 01:00:58,723
and rent a car.

1642
01:00:58,757 --> 01:01:00,057
Come back here
at 12:00 tonight

1643
01:01:00,090 --> 01:01:01,325
and pick up the boys,
and take them down

1644
01:01:01,358 --> 01:01:03,493
to gordon's warehouse
to pick up a package.

1645
01:01:03,527 --> 01:01:05,228
Then drive them back here.

1646
01:01:05,262 --> 01:01:06,663
Okay, mr. Blake.

1647
01:01:06,697 --> 01:01:09,400
He's got framed
rubber vomit on the wall.

1648
01:01:11,035 --> 01:01:12,903
You know what,
I should call mr. Blake

1649
01:01:12,937 --> 01:01:14,872
and tell him
how much I like him.

1650
01:01:17,942 --> 01:01:19,477
Hello, kitty?
This is jimmy,

1651
01:01:19,510 --> 01:01:21,045
remember me?
I'm your boyfriend.

1652
01:01:21,078 --> 01:01:22,380
You'd better be.

1653
01:01:22,413 --> 01:01:23,815
Can I see you tonight?
We'll go dancing.

1654
01:01:23,848 --> 01:01:25,617
Oh, this is late-night hot.

1655
01:01:25,650 --> 01:01:26,883
Oh, swell.

1656
01:01:26,917 --> 01:01:28,485
I've got a little business
to take care of,

1657
01:01:28,518 --> 01:01:30,253
and I'll be about
half an hour late.

1658
01:01:30,287 --> 01:01:31,988
I've got something
awfully important to ask you.

1659
01:01:32,022 --> 01:01:34,425
Now, don't tell me
you're going to propose to me.

1660
01:01:34,458 --> 01:01:36,460
- Maybe.
- All right, hon,
I'll be looking for you.

1661
01:01:36,493 --> 01:01:38,963
Jimmy's cheating on me!

1662
01:01:38,997 --> 01:01:42,167
That guy's eaves-dropping
on his eaves-dropping.

1663
01:01:42,200 --> 01:01:43,533
Wait here, I'll be back
in an hour.

1664
01:01:43,567 --> 01:01:45,368
With squeaky shoes on.

1665
01:01:49,740 --> 01:01:51,908
[Joel]
♪ love came between us ♪

1666
01:01:54,245 --> 01:01:55,580
Quack, quack.
Quack-quack quack.

1667
01:01:55,613 --> 01:01:58,015
Oh, hello. I didn't expect
to see you, charlie.

1668
01:01:58,048 --> 01:02:00,050
I know you didn't.
You expected the kid.

1669
01:02:00,083 --> 01:02:02,687
Nobody expects
to see charlie!

1670
01:02:02,720 --> 01:02:05,055
♪ Love came between us ♪

1671
01:02:05,088 --> 01:02:06,623
Oh, uh, buttermints, huh?

1672
01:02:06,657 --> 01:02:09,427
Don't mind if I do. Mmm.

1673
01:02:09,460 --> 01:02:12,363
First of all, you and I are
gonna straighten out something.

1674
01:02:12,397 --> 01:02:14,132
What's going on
between you two?

1675
01:02:14,165 --> 01:02:15,933
Uh, cheap love. Why?

1676
01:02:15,967 --> 01:02:17,835
I don't know what you're
talking about, charlie.

1677
01:02:17,868 --> 01:02:19,970
Why is she dressed like
major barbara?

1678
01:02:20,003 --> 01:02:21,538
No?

1679
01:02:21,572 --> 01:02:23,507
- Well, I'll make it clear.
- [Joel mumbles]

1680
01:02:23,540 --> 01:02:26,677
I heard that phone conversation
you had a little while ago.

1681
01:02:26,710 --> 01:02:28,245
He was talking
from my office.

1682
01:02:28,278 --> 01:02:30,047
It was funny.
Made me laugh-- hah!

1683
01:02:30,080 --> 01:02:32,283
So you really
fell in love with the kid.

1684
01:02:32,317 --> 01:02:34,152
Now, look.

1685
01:02:34,185 --> 01:02:36,453
Nobody's gonna
take you away from me.

1686
01:02:36,487 --> 01:02:38,455
- Nobody.
- Not even me, see?

1687
01:02:38,488 --> 01:02:39,857
I'll kill me
before that happens.

1688
01:02:39,890 --> 01:02:42,227
Why... why, charlie.

1689
01:02:42,260 --> 01:02:45,128
You don't really think
I fell for that kid, do you?

1690
01:02:45,162 --> 01:02:47,063
Why, you asked me
to string him along.

1691
01:02:47,097 --> 01:02:48,632
Can I help it
if he fell for me?

1692
01:02:48,665 --> 01:02:51,968
Well, he did win
that essay contest.

1693
01:02:52,002 --> 01:02:53,437
He's as good as forgotten.

1694
01:02:53,470 --> 01:02:56,273
[All] ♪ liar! Liar! ♪

1695
01:02:56,307 --> 01:02:58,808
When he gets here,
I want you to get rid of him.

1696
01:02:58,842 --> 01:03:01,012
- Your way.
- Or the highway.

1697
01:03:01,045 --> 01:03:03,380
Or would you rather
have me do it?

1698
01:03:03,413 --> 01:03:04,682
Okay, charlie.

1699
01:03:04,715 --> 01:03:06,150
I'll be happy in my work.

1700
01:03:06,183 --> 01:03:07,885
It ought to be a cinch.

1701
01:03:07,918 --> 01:03:11,088
- [Door buzzes]
- Oh, it's the three
hard-boiled eggs she ordered.

1702
01:03:11,122 --> 01:03:12,357
I'll be in there listening.

1703
01:03:12,390 --> 01:03:15,325
Like I usually am.

1704
01:03:15,358 --> 01:03:16,960
Watch out! Aah!

1705
01:03:16,993 --> 01:03:19,363
- [All mimic crash]
- [Doorbell buzzes]

1706
01:03:21,265 --> 01:03:24,102
[Servo muffled]
Hey, I thought you were gonna
have this stuff dry-cleaned.

1707
01:03:24,135 --> 01:03:26,237
Well, aren't I miss popular?

1708
01:03:28,605 --> 01:03:30,373
Well, I've joined
the black hand. Hi!

1709
01:03:30,407 --> 01:03:31,908
--Let's get going.
We've only got a few hours.

1710
01:03:31,942 --> 01:03:34,478
I have some work to do
later on.

1711
01:03:34,512 --> 01:03:36,213
I'm not going.

1712
01:03:36,247 --> 01:03:39,350
Well, what the--
wait a minute!

1713
01:03:39,383 --> 01:03:41,252
Hey, are you kidding?
Why, over the phone,

1714
01:03:41,285 --> 01:03:42,820
you just got through
saying we'd go someplace.

1715
01:03:42,853 --> 01:03:45,355
[Joel as schwarzenegger]
I lied.

1716
01:03:45,388 --> 01:03:46,757
I know,
but after I talked to you,

1717
01:03:46,790 --> 01:03:48,592
- I changed my mind.
- Guy in the closet.

1718
01:03:48,625 --> 01:03:49,993
An old friend of mine called,

1719
01:03:50,027 --> 01:03:51,828
- and I'm going out with him.
- Guy in the closet.

1720
01:03:51,862 --> 01:03:53,130
Hey, you say that so
convincingly,

1721
01:03:53,163 --> 01:03:54,698
I almost believe it.

1722
01:03:54,732 --> 01:03:56,067
[Crow muffled]
Hey, where'd you get
these golf clubs?

1723
01:03:56,100 --> 01:03:57,268
- Shh!
- You can believe it.

1724
01:03:57,302 --> 01:03:58,635
Guy in the closet.

1725
01:03:58,668 --> 01:03:59,970
- Do you mean it?
- Closet.

1726
01:04:00,003 --> 01:04:01,972
Of course I mean it.

1727
01:04:02,005 --> 01:04:03,440
Hey, I smell italian.

1728
01:04:03,473 --> 01:04:05,108
- Look, wh--
- oh, you poor chump.

1729
01:04:05,142 --> 01:04:06,477
[Crow as bert lahr]
Courage!

1730
01:04:06,510 --> 01:04:09,280
Did you really
take me seriously?

1731
01:04:09,313 --> 01:04:11,215
Did you think for one minute
that I loved you?

1732
01:04:11,248 --> 01:04:12,883
That I wanted to marry you?

1733
01:04:12,917 --> 01:04:14,185
She's smokin'.

1734
01:04:14,218 --> 01:04:15,687
