- No.
- I found a toenail
in my hamburger.

2223
01:23:16,658 --> 01:23:18,227
I thought you liked it here
pretty well.

2224
01:23:18,260 --> 01:23:19,395
Seem to be settling down.

2225
01:23:19,428 --> 01:23:21,230
I do like it, al.
It's not that.

2226
01:23:21,263 --> 01:23:23,298
In fact, it's the only time
I've ever really been happy.

2227
01:23:23,332 --> 01:23:25,302
But I want a salad.
Is that asking too much?

2228
01:23:25,335 --> 01:23:28,170
Spill it, son,
you can tell me.

2229
01:23:28,203 --> 01:23:29,572
Well, it's-- it's just
that I've been

2230
01:23:29,605 --> 01:23:30,973
thinking things over,
that's all.

2231
01:23:31,007 --> 01:23:32,308
- And I want new curtains.
- You wanna go back

2232
01:23:32,342 --> 01:23:34,243
and straighten yourself out?

2233
01:23:34,277 --> 01:23:36,880
Square accounts?
Take the load off your mind?

2234
01:23:36,913 --> 01:23:38,147
Yeah, I guess that's it.

2235
01:23:38,180 --> 01:23:39,948
Bring your trousers
in for dry-cleaning?

2236
01:23:39,982 --> 01:23:41,250
Find the courage to do it.

2237
01:23:41,283 --> 01:23:42,418
Change that old underwear?

2238
01:23:42,452 --> 01:23:43,687
Would you help me, al?

2239
01:23:43,720 --> 01:23:45,020
And don't mention god.

2240
01:23:45,053 --> 01:23:47,023
I've been waiting
to hear you say that, son.

2241
01:23:47,057 --> 01:23:49,058
So I prepared a song.

2242
01:23:49,092 --> 01:23:51,293
We'll go back
and face it together.

2243
01:23:51,327 --> 01:23:52,762
After they hear your story,

2244
01:23:52,795 --> 01:23:54,963
I'm positive they'll
give you a break.

2245
01:23:54,997 --> 01:23:56,398
Don't worry.

2246
01:23:56,432 --> 01:23:57,600
Ah, gee, that's swell.

2247
01:23:57,633 --> 01:23:59,068
Well, I feel better already.

2248
01:23:59,102 --> 01:24:01,772
Now tuck in to that beef.

2249
01:24:01,805 --> 01:24:04,107
You see, miss reed, I couldn't
let jimmy give himself up

2250
01:24:04,140 --> 01:24:06,375
unless he'd seen you first.

2251
01:24:06,408 --> 01:24:08,678
- Okay. Let's go.
- And I wanted to see
you too, jimmy.

2252
01:24:08,712 --> 01:24:10,247
To explain
and tell you the truth--

2253
01:24:10,280 --> 01:24:11,848
- I never wore the shoes.
- Blake was in

2254
01:24:11,882 --> 01:24:13,382
the other room that night,
listening.

2255
01:24:13,415 --> 01:24:15,285
I had to say what I did,
or he'd've killed you.

2256
01:24:15,318 --> 01:24:18,220
- Huh.
- They tried to the night
they beat you up.

2257
01:24:18,253 --> 01:24:20,490
And, then, the things
you said weren't true.

2258
01:24:20,523 --> 01:24:22,025
Of course they weren't true.

2259
01:24:22,058 --> 01:24:24,560
Except for about
your lousy shoe career.

2260
01:24:24,593 --> 01:24:25,962
Oh, jimmy, blake's the cause

2261
01:24:25,995 --> 01:24:27,530
of all your trouble
and mine, too.

2262
01:24:27,563 --> 01:24:29,965
If he finds out you're here,
he'll kill us both.

2263
01:24:29,998 --> 01:24:32,002
No, he won't, because he's going
to the police station with me.

2264
01:24:32,035 --> 01:24:33,603
You and al can call the cops
and follow us.

2265
01:24:33,637 --> 01:24:34,937
Jimmy, wait! Jimmy!

2266
01:24:34,970 --> 01:24:36,038
Quack, quack, quack quack.

2267
01:24:36,072 --> 01:24:38,942
Again, proving
just how stupid he is.

2268
01:24:38,975 --> 01:24:42,245
So, how about a little sugar
for happy chef over here?

2269
01:24:42,278 --> 01:24:43,580
Organized crime,
please hold.

2270
01:24:43,613 --> 01:24:45,248
Organized crime,
please hold-- sir?

2271
01:24:48,117 --> 01:24:50,687
Let me guess.
It's your birthday.

2272
01:24:50,720 --> 01:24:52,722
- Hello, jimmy.
- How's your hat? [Chuckles]

2273
01:24:52,755 --> 01:24:54,523
What brings you to see me?

2274
01:24:54,557 --> 01:24:56,192
Not in trouble again, are you?

2275
01:24:56,225 --> 01:24:57,593
No, but you are.

2276
01:24:57,627 --> 01:24:58,962
I'm giving myself up
to the police,

2277
01:24:58,995 --> 01:25:00,563
and you're coming with me.

2278
01:25:00,597 --> 01:25:01,898
You're taking a lot
for granted, aren't you?

2279
01:25:01,932 --> 01:25:03,432
Maybe I am.

2280
01:25:03,465 --> 01:25:06,202
But you're gonna tell everything
that's happened between us.

2281
01:25:06,235 --> 01:25:07,937
- And if I don't?
- You'll kill me?

2282
01:25:07,970 --> 01:25:09,972
The police are on their way
here to see that you do.

2283
01:25:10,005 --> 01:25:11,773
Now, let's see,
did I call them?... right.

2284
01:25:11,807 --> 01:25:14,677
Okay, jimmy.

2285
01:25:14,710 --> 01:25:18,047
About time I went on the
straight and narr-- hi-keeba!

2286
01:25:18,080 --> 01:25:21,885
Well, that's
a weird position.

2287
01:25:21,918 --> 01:25:25,688
They're really
going to town in there.

2288
01:25:25,722 --> 01:25:28,023
Hey, does anyone
have an appointment?

2289
01:25:31,293 --> 01:25:32,428
[Gunshot]

2290
01:25:32,462 --> 01:25:35,030
His heart just exploded.

2291
01:25:35,063 --> 01:25:36,765
Well, so much for the whole

2292
01:25:36,798 --> 01:25:38,635
"he's coming with me"
scenario.

2293
01:25:41,337 --> 01:25:43,472
Uh, I accuse my parents.

2294
01:25:45,375 --> 01:25:47,277
I tried to take the gun
away from him.

2295
01:25:47,310 --> 01:25:50,178
- But it went off.
- Huh?

2296
01:25:50,212 --> 01:25:52,348
Oh, I know I've lied.
I've cheated.

2297
01:25:52,382 --> 01:25:55,318
- I've done a lot of things
that I shouldn't have done.
- And more.

2298
01:25:55,352 --> 01:25:57,887
But maybe I wouldn't have
started lying to my schoolmates

2299
01:25:57,920 --> 01:26:00,423
if I hadn't been ashamed
of my home life.

2300
01:26:00,457 --> 01:26:03,358
If I hadn't been ashamed
that my parents were--

2301
01:26:03,392 --> 01:26:06,628
- were denying--
- this is wild.

2302
01:26:06,662 --> 01:26:10,433
--The love and protection
that a boy needs.

2303
01:26:10,467 --> 01:26:11,902
The guidance
that sets him straight.

2304
01:26:11,935 --> 01:26:15,170
Maybe they should've
sworn him in.

2305
01:26:15,203 --> 01:26:17,073
And that's why...

2306
01:26:17,107 --> 01:26:18,742
I accuse my parents.

2307
01:26:18,775 --> 01:26:21,143
[All] Aah. Oh.

2308
01:26:21,177 --> 01:26:22,978
Is your hat flask empty yet?

2309
01:26:23,012 --> 01:26:24,880
That court reporter
is dreamy.

2310
01:26:27,017 --> 01:26:29,018
Seeing as it's your birthday,
we'll let you go.

2311
01:26:29,052 --> 01:26:30,953
- James wilson--
- you dummy.

2312
01:26:30,987 --> 01:26:33,823
Your story is supported by much
of the evidence in this case.

2313
01:26:33,857 --> 01:26:36,525
And I think indicates clearly
that you are not guilty

2314
01:26:36,558 --> 01:26:38,027
of the killing
of charles blake.

2315
01:26:38,060 --> 01:26:39,362
Thanks! Well, bye.

2316
01:26:39,395 --> 01:26:40,797
--Count I find you
not guilty.

2317
01:26:40,830 --> 01:26:42,798
[Crowd murmurs]

2318
01:26:42,832 --> 01:26:44,767
Huh-- oh. Oh, "not" guilty!

2319
01:26:44,800 --> 01:26:47,170
- Oh.
- On the remaining counts

2320
01:26:47,203 --> 01:26:48,872
of having aided and abetted

2321
01:26:48,905 --> 01:26:50,507
in the transportation
and concealment

2322
01:26:50,540 --> 01:26:51,607
of stolen property,

2323
01:26:51,640 --> 01:26:53,308
- uh-oh.
- I find you guilty

2324
01:26:53,342 --> 01:26:55,545
and sentence you
to five years in state prison.

2325
01:26:55,578 --> 01:26:56,912
Hey, my dad went there.

2326
01:26:56,945 --> 01:26:58,513
That sentence
is hereby suspended.

2327
01:26:58,547 --> 01:27:00,650
And you are placed
on probation for two years.

2328
01:27:00,683 --> 01:27:02,452
- Thank god I'm white!
- You are to remain in

2329
01:27:02,485 --> 01:27:05,020
the custody of your parents
until you are 21.

2330
01:27:05,053 --> 01:27:06,322
During which time I hope

2331
01:27:06,355 --> 01:27:07,823
that you will
justify the confidence

2332
01:27:07,857 --> 01:27:09,158
- I am placing in you.
- Hah!

2333
01:27:09,192 --> 01:27:10,493
I will, your honor.

2334
01:27:10,527 --> 01:27:13,595
Oh, let's go to jack taylor's
and celebrate.

2335
01:27:13,628 --> 01:27:15,063
- Jimmy!
- Wait, wait,

2336
01:27:15,097 --> 01:27:17,433
he has to talk
to doug llewelyn first.

2337
01:27:23,172 --> 01:27:24,707
He accused us.

2338
01:27:24,740 --> 01:27:27,577
Why don't you just
do it on the bench?

2339
01:27:27,610 --> 01:27:29,612
As for you,
mr. and mrs. Wilson.

2340
01:27:29,645 --> 01:27:31,380
You are not on trial here.

2341
01:27:31,413 --> 01:27:33,548
But you have seen
the tragedy brought about

2342
01:27:33,582 --> 01:27:35,318
by the neglect
your boy suffered.

2343
01:27:35,352 --> 01:27:36,785
You will roast in hell.

2344
01:27:36,818 --> 01:27:38,788
--The only parents
guilty of such neglect.

2345
01:27:38,822 --> 01:27:41,323
- I speak
to parents everywhere--
- message coming in!

2346
01:27:41,357 --> 01:27:43,025
- There it is.
- In the pursuit
of your own

2347
01:27:43,058 --> 01:27:44,760
--own pleasures
and occupations,

2348
01:27:44,793 --> 01:27:46,428
you neglect your children.

2349
01:27:46,462 --> 01:27:48,530
Realize now
before it is too late.

2350
01:27:48,563 --> 01:27:50,633
- Buy bonds.
- This might have been your boy.

2351
01:27:50,667 --> 01:27:51,767
Not that your boy would be

2352
01:27:51,800 --> 01:27:53,670
quite so thick-headed
as jimmy.

2353
01:27:53,703 --> 01:27:55,372
I accuse my parents

2354
01:27:55,405 --> 01:27:58,607
brought to you
by boone's farm.

2355
01:27:58,640 --> 01:28:01,277
The makers of this film
also accuse hitler

2356
01:28:01,310 --> 01:28:03,112
and tojo and mussolini!

2357
01:28:03,145 --> 01:28:05,280
We accuse them all.
Soon we'll accuse stalin.

2358
01:28:05,313 --> 01:28:06,915
Seriously, joel,
who would you accuse?

2359
01:28:06,948 --> 01:28:09,985
Oh, I don't really...

2360
01:28:21,730 --> 01:28:24,400
Okay, as we move
into the home stretch,

2361
01:28:24,433 --> 01:28:26,202
I thought it'd be nice
to read a letter.

2362
01:28:26,235 --> 01:28:28,303
So...

2363
01:28:28,337 --> 01:28:29,972
Uh, hi, tom. Hi, crow.

2364
01:28:30,005 --> 01:28:31,373
Just getting ready
to read a letter.

2365
01:28:31,407 --> 01:28:33,075
Oh, no thank you, that's okay.

2366
01:28:33,108 --> 01:28:35,512
All we'd like is
just a cup of coffee.

2367
01:28:35,545 --> 01:28:37,813
[Cough] Hamburgers. [Cough]

2368
01:28:37,847 --> 01:28:39,515
Well, I'll just get going
on this letter, then.

2369
01:28:39,548 --> 01:28:40,683
Hamburgers. [Cough]

2370
01:28:40,717 --> 01:28:43,252
No, no thanks.
We're... not hungry?

2371
01:28:43,285 --> 01:28:45,622
Oh, I get it.
It's like in the movie.

2372
01:28:45,655 --> 01:28:48,257
How would you boys
like a hamburger?

2373
01:28:48,290 --> 01:28:49,492
Like that?

2374
01:28:49,525 --> 01:28:51,627
Finally, what
took you so long?

2375
01:28:51,660 --> 01:28:53,195
What a maroon.

2376
01:28:53,228 --> 01:28:54,830
Now.

2377
01:28:54,863 --> 01:28:56,598
Now what?

2378
01:28:56,632 --> 01:28:58,067
- [Bots sigh]
- No, no, no.

2379
01:28:58,100 --> 01:28:59,902
You stupid, stupid man.

2380
01:28:59,935 --> 01:29:01,203
Now, you present us

2381
01:29:01,237 --> 01:29:03,538
with a big, beefy char-broiled
hamburger "sammich"

2382
01:29:03,572 --> 01:29:06,175
and a french-fried potatoes
garnish like in the movie.

2383
01:29:06,208 --> 01:29:08,443
Uh, all I got
is this postcard.

2384
01:29:08,477 --> 01:29:10,312
D'oh. Crow, you talk to him.

2385
01:29:10,345 --> 01:29:12,815
You were supposed to get us

2386
01:29:12,848 --> 01:29:14,817
a char-broiled
hamburger sandwich

2387
01:29:14,850 --> 01:29:16,018
like in the movie.

2388
01:29:16,052 --> 01:29:19,555
[Sobs] What is happening
to this family?

2389
01:29:19,588 --> 01:29:21,057
Come on, honey.
Honey, honey.

2390
01:29:21,090 --> 01:29:22,858
There must be a pie cooling
in the ship someplace.

2391
01:29:22,892 --> 01:29:25,160
- A pie?
- It's just a movie, guys.

2392
01:29:25,193 --> 01:29:27,197
Jeez.

2393
01:29:29,832 --> 01:29:31,133
Anyway.

2394
01:29:31,167 --> 01:29:33,202
Thought we could
read this letter now.

2395
01:29:33,235 --> 01:29:34,903
Um, this says,

2396
01:29:34,937 --> 01:29:37,038
"for rent,
the barco rammer."

2397
01:29:37,072 --> 01:29:38,842
And it's from peter spears.

2398
01:29:38,875 --> 01:29:40,075
And on the back here--

2399
01:29:40,108 --> 01:29:41,910
let's put that on still store
in the back.

2400
01:29:41,943 --> 01:29:43,847
It says, "the barco rammer.

2401
01:29:43,880 --> 01:29:45,548
"Indisputably the finest.

2402
01:29:45,582 --> 01:29:48,317
"It will ram, it will pound,
it will press.

2403
01:29:48,350 --> 01:29:50,285
It will do what
you want it to do."

2404
01:29:50,318 --> 01:29:51,853
And then
he humorously writes,

2405
01:29:51,887 --> 01:29:53,857
"the perfect date
for crow and tom."

2406
01:29:53,890 --> 01:29:56,925
Which I thought
was pretty... funny?

2407
01:29:56,958 --> 01:29:59,795
[Tank ratchets, clanks]

2408
01:30:02,632 --> 01:30:04,833
I accuse you, joel.

2409
01:30:04,867 --> 01:30:07,035
Now, carefully.

2410
01:30:07,068 --> 01:30:09,972
Hand over
the hamburger sandwich.

2411
01:30:12,040 --> 01:30:13,408
Ahh.

2412
01:30:13,442 --> 01:30:14,610
Don't let him forget
the french-fried

2413
01:30:14,643 --> 01:30:16,312
- potatoes garnish.
- Right.

2414
01:30:16,345 --> 01:30:19,015
Joel, you magnificent bastard!
I read your menu!

2415
01:30:19,048 --> 01:30:21,150
Come on, we gotta beat
mighty messina, maggot!

2416
01:30:21,183 --> 01:30:22,785
Aah.

2417
01:30:26,455 --> 01:30:28,090
Uh, what do you think, sirs?

2418
01:30:28,123 --> 01:30:30,660
[Glass breaks]

2419
01:30:30,693 --> 01:30:33,395
[Stripper coughs]

2420
01:30:35,732 --> 01:30:37,633
Uh, sorry, joel.
Didn't catch that.

2421
01:30:37,667 --> 01:30:39,868
We, uh, came this close
to losing...

2422
01:30:39,902 --> 01:30:41,703
- Rodney.
- Right, right.

2423
01:30:41,737 --> 01:30:43,372
Almost lost rodney.

2424
01:30:43,405 --> 01:30:44,907
Is this enough, doctor f?

2425
01:30:44,940 --> 01:30:47,477
No way, frank. There's plenty
more frosting to shovel.

2426
01:30:47,510 --> 01:30:51,013
Oh, just go push the button,
you freaked-out maniac.

2427
01:30:51,047 --> 01:30:52,548
Uh, look, rodney.

2428
01:30:52,582 --> 01:30:54,883
I'm sorry this whole thing
got out of hand.

2429
01:30:54,917 --> 01:30:57,453
I'd like to make it
worth your while.

2430
01:30:57,487 --> 01:30:59,288
Oh, no, that's--
that's all right.

2431
01:30:59,322 --> 01:31:01,057
That-- you've done enough.

2432
01:32:04,287 --> 01:32:07,088
[Dad laughs]

2433
01:32:08,223 --> 01:32:10,560
Well, what's so funny?

2434
01:32:13,728 --> 01:32:15,397
This has been
a presentation

2435
01:32:15,430 --> 01:32:16,998
from comedy central.

